==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|j}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|fi|jompi kumpi}}

===Etymology===
From {{m|fi|jompi}} and {{m|fi|kumpi}} &ndash; which are related to the stems ''jo-'' and ''-ku-''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{fi-IPA|jompi-kumpi}}
* {{hyphenation|fi|jom|pi|kum|pi}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|fi|pronoun|cat2=indefinite pronouns}}

# {{lb|fi|indefinite}} [[either|Either]] [[one]] (''of two things'').
#: {{ux|fi|'''Jompikumpi''' teistä valehtelee.|'''Either one''' of you lies.}}

====Usage notes====
* ''Jompikumpi'' also has plural forms, which are used e.g. with words that are only used in the plural: '''jommatkummat''' [[häät]], '''either one''' of the weddings.

====Declension====
* Both the parts are declined.

